  "summary": "Labour's Sadiq Khan was elected Mayor of London, succeeding the Conservative Boris Johnson after eight years. Khan won 1,148,716 first-preference votes (44.2%) to Conservative Zac Goldsmith's 909,755 (35.0%), extending his lead to 1,310,143 against 994,614 after second preferences were redistributed. Khan won the highest number and share of first preferences of any mayoral candidate to that point. Labour again took 12 of the 25 Assembly seats and remained the largest party.",
